' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
'
' #####  v6.4.5 (Unofficial) ##### 20230827
'
' - Modified the conpiler (xcol.x) so that when a call to a CFUNCTION is made,
'   the stack pointer (rsp) will be adjusted to a 128-bit boundary before the function
'   is called and restored to the original value after the CFUNCTION returns.
'   Corrected errors compiling binary code for passing argument to registers r8 and r9.
'
' #####  v6.4.4 (Unofficial) ##### 20230731
'
' - Modified the conpiler (xcol.x) so that when a call to an EXTERNAL CFUNCTION is made in a user program
'   the 64-bit address of the function is moved to the rax register followed by a call *%rax.
'      movabsq 0x0000FED77524DF50,%rax
'      call    *%rax
'
' #####  v6.4.3 (Unofficial) ##### 20230407
'
' - Modified the function XuiFont() so that when the "view font" button is pushed,
'   "Font Nonexistant" will be displayed if the font criteria cannot be found.
'   This should make the demo program tfont.x more usefule for a person using it
'   to choose a font that he might want to use in a program.
'
' #####  v6.4.2 (Unofficial) ##### 20230201
'
' - Segment violations occurred when run on Debian 10 when X11 functuions where called
'   with the stack pointer (rsp) not set to a 128-bit boundary. Two new functions are
'   used to adjust the rsp before calling the X11 function: XxxRspEven() and XxxRspOdd()
'   XxxRspEven() is used if 6 or less, 8, 10, or 12 variables are being passed.
'   XxxRspOdd() is used if 7, 9, or 11 variables are being passed.
'   In the following example code, 12 variables are being passed to the C-function XGetWindowProperty;
'   6 are put in cpu registers and 6 (an EVEN number) are pushed on the stack, so XxxRspEven is used.
'   If it modifies the rsp, it returns a value of 8 to rspMod,
'   After the X11 function XGetWindowProperty is called, rspMod is checked to see if XxxRestoreRsp
'   should be called to put the rsp register back to the original value.
'
'			rspMod = XxxRspEven ()
'			error = XGetWindowProperty (sdisplay, swindow, #XA_TEXT, offset, length, delete, #XA_STRING, &rtype, &format, &items, &after, &data)
'			IF rspMod THEN XxxRestoreRsp ()
'
' #####  v6.4.1 (Unofficial) ##### 20220901
'
' - Thousands of changes made to enable Xbasic to run in 64-bit mode.
' - The executable file is called xb64
'
' #####  v6.3.26 (Unofficial) ##### 20180608
'
